# Cloudflare Workers static assets header rules. Applies to everything the
# assets layer serves (including the single-page-application index.html
# fallback); worker responses (/api/*, /releases/*) set their own headers in
# code. Rules are cumulative — a later matching block must detach a header
# before setting a new value ("! Cache-Control").
#
# The policy, matching how large SPA + API deployments ship:
# - HTML and unhashed files (service worker, manifest, theme-init, icons,
#   fonts): never cached without revalidation. This is what makes every
#   deploy reach users on their next load.
# - Vite content-hashed assets: immutable for a year. New content always
#   ships under a new URL, so a long TTL is safe and free of staleness.
#   Only content-hashed URLs may be immutable — never index.html.
# - Deploys are atomic: Workers publishes every file together, so HTML never
#   references missing or mixed-revision assets; no ?v= cache-busting
#   (revisions ride inside the SW precache keys, not the network URLs).

/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/sw.js
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

/assets/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
